# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button on
# the repo page, and Zenodo reads it when minting the DOI.
#
# doi is the version DOI for the release named in version; the concept DOI
# under identifiers always resolves to the newest release. Cite the version in
# a paper, the concept when you mean the software in general.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use basinkit in published work, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying datasets. Basin.license_report() prints those."
title: "basinkit: basin-scale acquisition of open Earth observation data"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that turns a coordinate on any river into an analysis-ready
  basin package. It returns the upstream basin polygon; open Earth observation
  layers clipped and masked to that polygon rather than to its bounding box;
  the profile of the river arriving at the point, with its long profile and the
  tributaries that feed it; and the classical Horton-Strahler-Schumm
  morphometry, with streams counted as Strahler streams rather than as the
  reaches a river dataset splits them into. Nineteen datasets are reachable
  without an account, login or credential. Delineation is validated blind
  against agency-published catchment areas at 2,550 gauges in 99 countries on
  six continents, with the accuracy reported by catchment size rather than as a
  single figure.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Pradeepika
    family-names: Kaushik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0767-3983"
version: 0.9.2
# 10.5281/zenodo.23426122 is 0.9.1's version DOI and is not true of this
# release. Until Zenodo mints one for 0.9.2 the concept DOI is the only
# correct answer here; replace this with the 0.9.2 version DOI once it exists.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22181933"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23426122"
    description: "Version DOI -- the previous release, 0.9.1"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22181933"
    description: "Concept DOI -- always resolves to the latest version"
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Praddy-GByte/basinkit"
url: "https://github.com/Praddy-GByte/basinkit"
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - river basin
  - morphometry
  - geomorphology
  - drainage network
  - strahler order
  - watershed delineation
  - remote sensing
  - earth observation
  - open data
  - gis
